{
 "schema": "singlet.benchmark.capability",
 "schema_version": "1.1.0",
 "capability": "donor-snps",
 "title": "Donor SNP genotypes (metrics only)",
 "conclusion": "At sites with >= 10 reads, Singlet's donor genotypes agree with truth at 0.961 over the held-out pools (vireo 0.978, cellsnp-pileup 0.993); truth is replicate-lane RNA genotypes (Kang) and 1000 Genomes genotypes (cell lines). Genotypes themselves are not published.",
 "methods": "Truth is real. For the Kang lanes (no public genotypes exist) it is the genotype of each donor called from RNA reads of a second library of the same donors (batch 2: control and IFN-beta lanes; batch 1: lanes A and B against lane C), pooling the cells that the authors' demuxlet labelled as that donor, with a fixed binomial model (error 0.01, flat prior, posterior >= 0.99). For two cell-line pools it is the 1000 Genomes high-coverage genotypes of the cell lines' donors (HG00362, HG01277 as one-donor libraries; GM12878 + GM18502 as a real 1:1 mixture). Singlet runs end to end with its automatic donor count and the default 1000G panel (AF >= 5%); its per-donor genotypes are those of its own clusters. Vireo (K given) and souporcell (k given) are run on the same BAM, cells and panel; cellsnp-pileup genotypes the pooled reads of vireo's clusters (all cells for one-donor libraries). Clusters are matched to truth donors by cell overlap (Kang) or by genotype agreement (1000G). Concordance is the fraction of sites with a truth genotype and a tool call at which the genotype class (0/0, 0/1, 1/1) is identical; the dp10 stratum keeps sites where the tool's own donor-level depth is >= 10. Non-reference concordance and false-alt rate split the same table by truth class. The rule is match-or-beat against the best competitor, zero tolerance. No genotype, SNP or per-site count is published.",
 "status": "final",
 "generated_at": "2026-10-26T10:44:43+00:00",
 "owner": "pipeline-benchmark",
 "singlet": {
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "commit": "02aa9b938b54e0f92bba00c44c07b883a8660aa2",
  "branch": "prod/campaign",
  "binary": "singlet-campaign",
  "binary_sha256": "261d3a50ed624572418d30489dfd58904323f6e0d8820bd5260dfe7fb5038e6c"
 },
 "tools": [
  {
   "name": "singlet",
   "version": "1.0.0",
   "role": "singlet",
   "params": "singlet-campaign POOL.1fq --ref-base /mnt/projects/debruinz_project/cellarium/reference --genome-dir /mnt/projects/debruinz_project/cellarium/reference/GRCh38-2024-A/star_2.7.11b --exons /mnt/projects/debruinz_project/cellarium/reference/GRCh38-2024-A/genes/genes.gtf --threads 16 --pipeline --n-donors -1 --tagged-bam possorted.bam --bam-sort-mode disk --output-format mtx --raw-matrix  (default SNP panel: 1000 Genomes phase 3, AF >= 5%, 7.35 M SNPs; --n-donors K only for the told-K comparison runs)"
  },
  {
   "name": "vireo",
   "version": "0.5.9",
   "role": "competitor",
   "url": "https://github.com/single-cell-genetics/vireo",
   "citation": "Huang et al. 2019, Genome Biol 20:273",
   "params": "cellsnp-lite as above, then vireo -c cellsnp -o OUT -N K -p 16 --randSeed {1,2,3} --noPlot (K = true K, defaults otherwise: nInit 50, doublet detection on); K estimate: vireo -N 12 --randSeed 1, K = donors holding >= 1% of cells"
  },
  {
   "name": "souporcell",
   "version": "2.5",
   "role": "competitor",
   "url": "https://github.com/wheaton5/souporcell",
   "citation": "Heaton et al. 2020, Nat Methods 17:615",
   "params": "souporcell_pipeline.py -i cells.bam -b barcodes.txt -f /mnt/projects/debruinz_project/cellarium/reference/GRCh38-2024-A/fasta/genome.fa -t 16 -o OUT -k K --common_variants genome1K.phase3.SNP_AF5e2.chr1toX.hg38.sorted.chrprefix.vcf  (K = true K; remapping with minimap2 and every other option at its default; cells.bam = Singlet's tagged BAM restricted to the called cells)"
  },
  {
   "name": "cellsnp-pileup",
   "version": "1.2.3",
   "role": "competitor",
   "url": "https://github.com/single-cell-genetics/cellsnp-lite",
   "params": "cellsnp-lite counts as above, summed over the cells of each cluster (vireo's labels; all cells for one-donor libraries), genotyped with the binomial model of the truth: error 0.01, flat prior, posterior >= 0.99"
  },
  {
   "name": "1000genomes-highcov",
   "version": "20220422",
   "role": "truth",
   "url": "https://www.internationalgenome.org/data-portal/data-collection/30x-grch38",
   "params": "phased SNV/INDEL/SV callset of 3,202 samples, GRCh38"
  },
  {
   "name": "kang-replicate-lane",
   "version": "n/a",
   "role": "truth",
   "params": "pooled reads of the donor's cells in a second library of the same donors, binomial genotyping (error 0.01, posterior >= 0.99)"
  }
 ],
