 "caveats": [
  "The genotypes, SNPs and per-site allele counts are private; the only artifact is a table of genotype-class counts.",
  "Kang truth genotypes are called from RNA reads of a second library of the same donors (no public Kang genotypes exist): they are expression-limited and share RNA artefacts (editing, allele-specific expression) with the tested pool, so concordance is a lower bound for accuracy at sites both libraries cover and says nothing about unexpressed sites.",
  "The 1000 Genomes truth is whole-genome sequencing of the cell-line donor; LCL-specific somatic differences from the reference individual exist but are small.",
  "The panel is 1000 Genomes SNPs with allele frequency >= 5% (7.35 M sites); every tool sees the same panel.",
  "Singlet emits a genotype at every covered panel site, however shallow, so its 'all' concordance includes 1-read sites; the dp10 metrics are the fair view for a user who filters.",
  "The plain pileup baseline (cellsnp-pileup) is not a donor-demultiplexing method; it genotypes pooled reads of vireo's clusters (all cells for one-donor libraries) with the model used for the Kang truth."
 ]
}
